# Files that run inside the Linux container must keep LF endings, whatever the
# host checkout does. On a Windows checkout core.autocrlf rewrites them to CRLF,
# COPY bakes that into the image, and the kernel then reads the shebang as
# "/bin/sh\r" -- an interpreter that does not exist. The container dies at start
# with `exec /entrypoint.sh failed: No such file or directory` (exit 127), which
# gives no hint at the real cause.
*.sh            text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh   text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
